WHY THE NEGATIVE ARM IS A SEPARATE BINARY, not a build flag: the mechanism is a build-tagged file pair
keyed on goexperiment.burroughsspawn, so dropping the experiment would also remove the spawn door and the
arms would differ in two variables. The stub keeps the door and removes only the notification.

THE DIFFERENCE IS CHECKABLE IN THE ARTIFACT (standing property 13), not merely in the build command:

  $ wasm-tools print c2_<arm>.wasm | awk '/\(func \$syscall\.Read /{f=1} f{print} f&&/^  \)$/{exit}' \
      | grep -c 'entersyscallblock\|exitsyscall'
  c2_present.wasm -> 2
  c2_absent.wasm  -> 0

REGISTERED READINGS this pair must reproduce (phase4/clause2-recon.md, "The discriminating pair"):
  mechanism present -> sibling B advanced, 10 of 10
  mechanism absent  -> sibling B delta 0, every run, n=3
A reconstruction that only passes the positive arm is a new green asserting nothing; the negative arm is
what makes it the same witness.
